<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Nampak raises interim shr, div up.</title>
<headline>Nampak raises interim shr, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   56.1	  vs  51.9</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     55.9	  vs  52.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 14.4	  vs  13.7</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   283.4	 vs  263.6</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   443.4	 vs  415.5</p>
<p>    Tax			 149.9	 vs  144.2</p>
<p>    Finance costs	   20.5	  vs  9.0</p>
<p>    Turnover		  3,656.9     vs  3,376.3</p>
<p>Div payable July 11</p>
<p>on register June 6</p>
<p>Full name: Nampak Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  10.1	  vs  7.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast half year earnings for the packaging group of 58 cents within a range of 57.0 to 58.0 cents. They expected the dividend at 14.7 cents within a range of 13.7 to 16.3 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
